✅ Add Digits – Point-wise Note

The problem is about repeatedly adding digits until a single digit is obtained.
Instead of using loops, we use a mathematical trick (Digital Root).
The result follows a modulo 9 pattern.


✅ Formula

If num == 0 → return 0
If num % 9 == 0 → return 9
Else → return num % 9
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

✅ Key Idea

Sum of digits of a number is equivalent to num % 9
Exception: when remainder is 0, answer should be 9 (not 0)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

✅ Complexity

Time: O(1)
Space: O(1)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

public int addDigits(int num) {
        if(num==0){
            return 0;
        }if(num%9==0){
            return 9;
        }
        return num%9;
        
    }
